<title>USA: Warner-Lambert Atorvastatin OK in UK, Germany.</title>
<headline>Warner-Lambert Atorvastatin OK in UK, Germany.</headline>
<dateline>MORRIS PLAINS, N.J. 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warner-Lambert Co said it received marketing approval in the United Kingdom and Germany for atorvastatin, a cholesterol lowering drug.</p>
<p>The new drug will be marketed as Lipitor (atorvastatin calcium tablets) in the U.K. and as Sortis in Germany, the company said.</p>
<p>Lipitor was discovered and developed by the Parke-Davis Research division of the company, it said.</p>
<p>Earlier this year, the company announced it entered into a collaborative agreement with Pfizer Inc to co-promote and continue the development of Lipitor in the United States and on a broad basis around the world.</p>
<p>The company said it would receive milestone payments under the agreement, including unspecified additional payments to be made this year.</p>
</text>
